      "comment": "PARCAE (8) was backed as if unbeatable on debut at Mornington and won as expected, starting at $1.45 and coming right away to score by 2.5 lengths. She's a nicely bred filly who should only improve and gets every hope from the low gate. HEADBANGER (3) was just fair first up at Sandown Hillside when hard in the market but wasn't beaten far. She has built a nice affinity for Cranbourne with a couple of big wins here and this looks a lovely race for her. SWEET VIXEN (7) resumes for her second campaign having shown good ability in three runs to date. She should go well. MILOS FILOS (2) resumes having won a handy race in town before a break, consider. SHAIME (1) has a big weight off a spell but has good ability and is in the mix.",
